# The CRLF twins are byte-compared fixtures, and the bytes ARE the test.
#
# The repository-root .gitattributes checks every text file out as LF on
# every platform, which is right for source and wrong for these four: a
# *.crlf.fixture whose CRs were rewritten to LF on checkout is no longer a
# CRLF file, and TestParseRelative_CRLFFixtureMatchesLFTwin would then be
# asserting LF == LF while reporting that CRLF is handled.
#
# -text means "never convert, in either direction". The guard in that test
# (it fails if the fixture has no CRLF in it) is the second line of defence;
# this is the first.
*.crlf.fixture -text
